      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FRIZZA (2) enjoyed the much better draw when he beat a smart line-up of three-year-olds for a 3.2m win at this circuit and distance last week. Gets the same barrier so could go back-to-back. WICKED CONFESSION (3) came from wider than this to beat some good mares in landing the Sue Kelly Ladyship Stakes here last week. Tackles the boys this time but draws well and is rarely out of the money over the mile. THE NITESHIFT (1) hasn't raced since his fifth in the Vicbred final in September but was readied with a trial win. Flies fresh with three wins and a placing from four tries and should get every chance from the ace draw. ITS CONFIDENTIAL (10) and SEASIDER (11) may need some luck from wide draws but both are good enough to feature if it comes their way.",
